ere  should be 10 to 12 hours of gameplay to  keep you occupied not including trophy  chasing so far ratchet and clank is  promising improved visuals new planets  bosses weapons and  updated control scheme if you're a big  fan of developer insomniac games you'd  probably also be glad to hear about  their upcoming third person adventure  game edge of nowhere which has been  announced as a VR exclusive at you out  next year the game have been built from  the ground up with VR in mind so this  should be one to keep an eye on despite  the slightly odd choice of combining VR  with a third-person perspective finally  today it's been confirmed street fighter  5 and any future iterations of street  fighter 5 will not make their way to the  Xbox one although the latest entry in  the fighting series was unveiled as a  PlayStation console exclusive Capcom has  a history of iterating it's street  fighter games over time it appears that  won't be the case this time around  speculation that something like super  street fighter 5 may appear on xbox one  was shot down by a representative from  Capcom who insisted the company has a  firm partnership with Sony so don't  expect to see the game hit xbox anytime  soon at least until Street Fighter six  lands let me know down in the comments  what you think of all the oculus  announcements and if your personally  came to get into VR and why or why not  you can head to gamespot we've got you  on the division and raise up potentially  buying oh yeah I guess somebody should  those are all the things that I wanted  to tell you about today do let me know  your thoughts and viewings in the  comments down below and join me in a  super special guest tomorrow for some  top 5 goodness
 

